  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing alternatives with communities in mining contexts in the Cusco region, Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to promote and defend individual and collective rights of women and men, and their grassroots social organisations, in the highland provinces of Peru&apos;s Cuzco region (Chumbivilcas, Espinar and Paruro). The context in this region is marked by socio-environmental conflict and a strong presence of extractive industries. The indigenous and rural farming communities face high levels of poverty, exclusion and violation of their human rights. The health of these local communities is negatively affected by heavy metals in contaminated water and community leaders face increasing criminalisation.</narrative>
  </description>
